From: marcho78 <marcho78@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/tegra: Share the reservation object of imported dma-bufs

tegra_bo_import() gives the GEM object of an imported dma-buf its own,
empty reservation object, where drm_gem_prime_import_dev() takes the
dma-buf's. drm_gem_plane_helper_prepare_fb() then finds no fence to
wait for, so flipping to a buffer that another driver is still rendering
into (nouveau, through Mesa's tegra driver) scans out a half-drawn
frame. Use the dma-buf's reservation object.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/gem.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/gem.c
index 436394e04..b088f942c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/gem.c
@@ -494,6 +494,12 @@ static struct tegra_bo *tegra_bo_import(struct drm_device *drm,
 	get_dma_buf(buf);
 	bo->dma_buf = buf;
 
+	/*
+	 * Share the exporter's reservation object, as drm_gem_prime_import()
+	 * does, so that page flips wait for the exporter's rendering.
+	 */
+	bo->gem.resv = buf->resv;
+
 	return bo;
 
 detach:
